  "notes": "Godan verb ending in つ: {建|た}たない, {建|た}ちます, {建|た}って, {建|た}てば.\n\nUSAGE:\nAn intransitive verb — the building itself is the subject (ビルが{建|た}つ). The transitive counterpart is {建|た}てる (to build something). Do not confuse with the homophone {立|た}つ (to stand up) or {経|た}つ (time passes), which use different kanji.\n\nTRANSITIVITY PAIR:\n- {建|た}つ (intransitive): A building is built / stands\n- {建|た}てる (transitive): Someone builds a building",
